  "change": "Preserve full creation sequence assigned by the existing ordered compute prologue when TG_SIZE IDs wrap after 2048 waves. Complete-M0 permutation inference remains first. Fallback requires TG_SIZE and ordered append; per-group mode requires one wave per group. Validate live M0 low16 against wrapped ID, preserving zero crawler requirement. No title/hash/vendor/profile toggles, changed atomics, invented counter values or relaxed authentication.",
  "research": {
    "primary_source": "https://www.amd.com/content/dam/amd/en/documents/radeon-tech-docs/programmer-references/CIK_3D_registers_v2.pdf",
    "register": "COMPUTE_DISPATCH_INITIATOR",
    "interpretation": "ORDERED_APPEND_ENBL enables guest wave-ID assignment; ORDERED_APPEND_MODE distinguishes per-wave and per-threadgroup identity. The candidate uses this emulator's existing prologue assignment, preserving its unbounded dispatch ordinal alongside its wrapped TG_SIZE identity. It does not infer order from Vulkan arrival.",
    "local_evidence": "The uploaded compute IR uses WorkgroupIndex plus local wave, masks with 2047, shifts by six and packs the TG_SIZE SGPR. The last successful native DS dispatch has 2013 waves and the rejected first phase has 2092 waves. Raw failed capture packets are not present in the archive, so direct native duplicate-ID inspection remains unavailable.",
    "remaining_scope": "Existing complete-M0 permutation inference remains first choice. Dispatch-derived fallback is gated on TG_SIZE plus ordered append, and per-group mode only with one wave per group. Every participating packet must match the assigned wrapped ID and zero crawler increment. Existing instruction, checkpoint, token, memory and wave-count checks remain. Arbitrary nonzero crawler strides, multiwave per-group ordered identities and all platform/game correctness are not claimed."
  },
